# Shared finbot data directory for the document EPS review app.
# Set this in your shell; the package does not load .env files.
# The review workflow does not require provider or AWS credentials.
FINBOT_DATA_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/finbot/data

# Direct evaluation providers only. Add real keys to your ignored .env file.
# Load them into your shell with: set -a; source .env; set +a
# The app and CLI do not read .env automatically. Never commit real keys.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Only needed for an Anthropic personal/service key that is not workspace-scoped:
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
# Direct configs: configs/openai-luna-6-prompt-v4.json and
# configs/anthropic-haiku-5-5-prompt-v4.json.

# Evaluation CLI only: uses the normal AWS SDK credential chain.
# Choose a preconfigured profile if the default credentials are not appropriate.
# AWS_PROFILE=your-profile
# Recommended eval: configs/bedrock-nova-2-lite-prompt-v4.json (plain text + images).
# Separate Luna model/profile and region: configs/bedrock-luna.json.
# Alternative v4 models: bedrock-claude-sonnet-4-6-prompt-v4.json,
# bedrock-kimi-k3-prompt-v4.json, bedrock-mistral-large-3-prompt-v4.json,
# bedrock-qwen3-vl-235b-prompt-v4.json under configs/. Paid runs are explicit.
# Never put AWS access keys in committed configuration or prompts.
